WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.430
- Finland is one of the
most interesting markets

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:07.760
in the world for somebody like
me because I'm unemotional,

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:12.760
meaning marketing to me is
just whether it's outdoor,

00:00:13.022 --> 00:00:18.022
or Google or Facebook or
Snapchat or Instagram or drawing

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:22.860
on a building or a flyer or television,

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.550
I'm just unemotional; I don't care.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:27.230
I don't love digital, I
don't like technology.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.740
I like attention because
if you have attention

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:31.990
then you can tell somebody
what you're about.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.984
In Finland, per capita,
the usage of Instagram

00:00:36.984 --> 00:00:41.040
and Facebook in comparison
to how much marketing money

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.630
is being put in there by
the companies in Finland

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:46.080
is one of the biggest
opportunities in the world.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.700
The citizens of this country are using

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.800
these platforms tremendously.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.440
The entrepreneurs are
building small, little things,

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.710
the problem is unlike America
where the entrepreneurs

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:57.543
are winning.

00:00:57.543 --> 00:01:01.140
So in America, every big
company is in deep shit.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:01.973
For real.

00:01:04.275 --> 00:01:07.280
Like every industry including
Pizza Hut and Dominoes,

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.990
big trouble because they're
spending money on television

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:12.560
and outdoor and direct
mail and little startups

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.800
are spending it on Facebook
and things of that nature

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.390
and it's happened overnight.

00:01:19.381 --> 00:01:22.150
(mumbling)

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:24.730
What happens here is
entrepreneurs start winning

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:27.603
in Finland and then they
realize how much it works

00:01:27.603 --> 00:01:31.760
and they leave because the
market's not the biggest market.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.860
So when they see how big
the arbitrage is on Facebook

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.320
they go to the Nordics, they go to Europe,

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.800
they go to the US.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.350
They go get funding in
the US and start up.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:44.810
What's that done is created a
very interesting environment

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:49.300
here in Finland, in my opinion,
which is the big companies

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:53.930
are wasting money on traditional
stuff that got them here.

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:58.070
The entrepreneurs are
spending money originally

00:01:58.070 --> 00:01:58.910
but then leave.

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.800
You have to understand why
I'm so in love with Facebook

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:01.650
and Instagram right now.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:02.960
It's a marketplace.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:03.880
There is no floor.

00:02:07.832 --> 00:02:10.050
When you buy an ad on Facebook,
if it doesn't work well

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.240
and you try to spend a
lot of money, it stops

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.620
because their most valuable
thing is the person's attention

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.930
and bad advertising is bad for them.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.960
Whereas, when you run a
bad print ad or radio ad,

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.160
they'll take your money.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.060
And so to me, there's
an enormous opportunity.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:32.690
Influencers, I mean, when
I think about fast casual

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:37.600
or food space like I would
probably map all 5,000 people

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:41.200
that matter on Instagram
in Finland and pay them

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.030
to give awareness to your restaurants.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:47.800
I think the arbitrage in this country...

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.370
That's why when you said all
locations here, I perked up.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.770
I was like okay, they're
gonna be very interested

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:53.751
in what I have to say.

00:02:53.751 --> 00:02:56.280
I would spend 90% of
your money on Facebook.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:03.070
Yeah, and I'll tell you why
because it's a moment in time.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:07.470
My energy is based on
resentment and regret.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:11.080
I'm very famous in my circles
for building my dad's liquor

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:14.970
store in 1996 from three
to 60 million with no money

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.630
because I figured out Google.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.230
But the true is it should've
been three to 200 million.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.830
I didn't spend enough on Google.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.280
Because marketplaces eventually correct.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.700
Right now, I know for four
dollars to seven dollars

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:31.720
I can get in front of a
thousand people in Finland

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:34.030
on Facebook and they're paying attention.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:36.630
In four years, it's gonna cost me 80

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:38.520
and they're not gonna be paying attention.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.700
That's it; moments in time.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.230
So not that I ever believe
spending 90% of any money

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:49.250
on anything is the right
idea other than if you're in

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.490
the real estate business,
if you're right about

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:55.990
the beach front property, in
that moment you should buy

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:56.823
all of it.

00:03:56.823 --> 00:03:59.070
It's okay not to do other projects.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:01.170
That's how I feel about
Facebook and Instagram right now

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:02.003
in this country.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:07.570
- [Man] Is it because
the average digital spend

00:04:07.570 --> 00:04:11.170
in Finland compared to average usage...

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:13.040
- Yes, that's exactly right.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.910
And unlike other markets
where the entrepreneurs

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:19.890
and the venture capital-based
companies fill the pipe

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:22.010
and get the prices up, people leave here.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.920
Got it?

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.530
That's the opportunity.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.070
That's why I'm here.

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:31.420
- [Man] Almost makes me think
that now that we're talking

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:35.280
about the no pizza concept,
should we actually be

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.740
considering or creating
the no pizza concept

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:43.740
and just export the buying
form and then the product?

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:49.860
You can produce it almost
anywhere, but you would actually

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.120
have a comfy space.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:56.810
You would just buy it
and consume it whole.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:59.910
- The leap there gets more
logistically and operationally.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:00.940
I think, at it's bare minimum...

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.450
Like for example, the 270 locations.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.320
What's that called again, I apologize?

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:07.785
The first pizza place?

00:05:07.785 --> 00:05:08.618
(mumbling)

00:05:08.618 --> 00:05:10.870
So C-O, K-O-T-I.

00:05:12.727 --> 00:05:13.930
What do you spend on marketing?

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:15.790
What do you spend your
marketing money on now

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.900
to make that company successful?

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:20.650
- [Man] How much is the spread now?

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:21.950
- [Woman] On TV?

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.620
- Anything, across the board, TV.

00:05:25.672 --> 00:05:29.580
- [Woman] TV, out of home
advertising, both digital

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.360
and out of home.
- Yep.

00:05:34.181 --> 00:05:35.431
- And then radio.
- Yep.

00:05:36.937 --> 00:05:39.069
(people talking over each other)

00:05:39.069 --> 00:05:40.887
- [Man] How much euros?

00:05:40.887 --> 00:05:42.420
- Three million.
- Three mill.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:44.140
- [Woman] Yeah, three, roughly.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:47.340
- And how much does TV get?
- 40%.

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:52.340
- And then out of home?
- Ten, 12.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:55.300
- And radio?
- Eight, ten.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:59.260
- And then digital.
- Digital, 35.

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:01.250
- And within digital, what is it?

00:06:04.936 --> 00:06:06.190
- [Woman] I can't give you an idea.

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:07.300
- No problem.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:11.410
To me, what I've seen over and over again,

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:14.740
before I convince the
founder of the board to move

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:19.226
the big numbers, usually the
35% is where I focus first

00:06:19.226 --> 00:06:23.630
because digital itself
has a lot of bad stuff

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:25.810
in the way that I think.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:30.030
There's traditional digital
and there's 2018 digital.

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:34.900
Most of my clients and a lot
of what I see in the world

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:38.848
spended on programmatic
and search and banner

00:06:38.848 --> 00:06:42.900
and not enough on social and influencer.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:46.680
And then there's the question
of are you doing sales

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:47.980
or are you doing branding?

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:51.120
Because that's a whole mix in itself.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.540
What's the ROY?

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:55.640
Is it a transactional
in-store foot traffic sale,

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:56.750
delivery sale?

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.980
How are you breaking up brand.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:02.530
Such a confusion, I've been
surprised now going through it

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:03.950
the last ten years.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:06.010
I'm surprised how many people
think they're marketing

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:07.710
but what they're doing is selling.

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:09.563
It's sales.

00:07:09.563 --> 00:07:12.354
Everything is based on well,
it cost us nine dollars

00:07:12.354 --> 00:07:14.930
on Google to get this ten dollar pizza.

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:16.770
We make three dollars
profit, that's not good.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:17.710
What's the LTV?

00:07:19.664 --> 00:07:21.530
And they're not thinking about the brand

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:24.510
or the long tail or the
arbitrage of creative

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:27.200
or all the other variables
that actually play out.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:32.590
I don't buy Nike's because of
a sale, I buy it because it

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:36.800
won on brand and I think a lot about that.

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:39.210
And then how do you
replicate what you're...

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:42.150
To me, the biggest opportunity
for you is to figure out

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:45.520
how Facebook three-minute,
two-minute, one-minute videos

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.930
subsidize what you're doing on television.

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:50.820
Once you've figured that
out, I think you'd be stunned

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:53.040
by the ROY.
- Explain again.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.200
- I think what you're doing on...

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.560
Well actually, let me take a step back.

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:58.750
On television, are you doing
what I see a lot of QSR

00:07:58.750 --> 00:07:59.583
companies doing?

00:07:59.583 --> 00:08:02.060
Are you doing promotional advertising,

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:04.330
or are you doing brand?
- Both.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:07.300
- What would you say is the 50/50, 80/20?

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:08.870
What's your gut tell you?

00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:13.750
- [Woman] Well, now recently
it has been let's say 75/25.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:14.840
- Promotional.
- Brand.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.240
- Brand, great.

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:21.240
So, you know, to me my belief
is that in this country

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:27.090
specifically that the
amount of actual consumption

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:31.010
of the commercial is far less
than the way it's reported.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:35.340
That the math, I don't know if
you're using an internal MMM

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:39.390
or how you're scoring the
success of your television,

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:42.780
but the most sophisticated
scores of television

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:47.780
in the US and Europe and
other parts, they're making

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:53.090
too many assumptions of
consumption of commercials.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:56.590
The reason they say it works
is just the shear amount

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:57.840
of money that they spend.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:00.863
You know.

00:09:00.863 --> 00:09:04.300
I had one friend, I asked
him to just turn it off.

00:09:05.758 --> 00:09:07.250
I just didn't feel the effects of business

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:08.350
that much at all.

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:10.460
To me, I have a lot of clients.

00:09:12.491 --> 00:09:16.130
I had a meeting in the US
and she says well, Gary,

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:18.960
you know I do this, and she
goes Gary, but it didn't work.

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:21.260
Digital didn't work, television worked.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:22.830
I go okay.

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:27.500
I just know that that's not
true 99 out of 100 times.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.430
So I said let's talk, like
I said, in the same way

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:31.860
like give me the details.

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:34.990
And she smiled, she's
amazing I like her a lot,

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:37.750
she smiled so I already
knew I was in good shape.

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:38.830
She said okay.

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:40.020
I go what were the results?

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:41.210
What did you do in the first?

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:42.890
She said, it didn't work.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:44.120
I said, how do you know?

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:47.270
She said well in the
first quarter of this year

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:49.030
we did digital.

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:52.550
I go okay and she goes in
the last quarter we did TV.

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:55.880
So first I jumped on the fact
that liquor sales in the US,

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:58.340
50% of it is done in the fourth quarter

00:09:58.340 --> 00:09:59.860
versus the first quarter,
but that wasn't even it.

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:01.190
I thought that was my a-ha.

00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:03.970
That was nothing compared
to the next thing she said.

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:07.350
She said we spent 484
thousand dollars on digital

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:08.860
in the first quarter.

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:11.290
They spent 8.5 million on television.

00:10:14.436 --> 00:10:16.776
It's very interesting how
people want to protect

00:10:16.776 --> 00:10:19.330
what they know, or what got them there.

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:23.190
I think Facebook videos...

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:25.140
First of all, a couple things.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:26.530
Here's what I don't like about television

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:28.650
and why I'm obsessed about Facebook.

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:31.500
First, I think more people, if
you spent ten million dollars

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:34.420
or a million, if you spent a
million dollars on television,

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:36.980
you spent a million dollars
on Facebook video ads,

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:40.060
I think that more people would
actually see the Facebook.

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:41.340
That's number one.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:42.940
Like actually see it.

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:46.100
Number two, here's the
most important part,

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:48.610
there's a very big difference
between somebody who makes

00:10:48.610 --> 00:10:52.090
150 thousand euros a
year living in Helsinki

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:55.617
and somebody who makes 42
thousand euros living in a suburb

00:10:55.617 --> 00:10:58.530
of how they're gonna associate your brand

00:10:58.530 --> 00:11:00.890
and what value your pizza brings to them.

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:04.360
The fact that television
only allows you one piece

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:08.267
of creative, versus the fact
that Facebook can target

00:11:08.267 --> 00:11:13.100
very specifically and you're
able to make eight pieces

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:17.030
of creative, if you're 62 and you're 29,

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:19.470
I have a funny feeling your brand, Koti,

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.020
means something different.

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:23.640
Your television is just doing one message.

00:11:26.845 --> 00:11:29.730
It's the flexibility of scaled context

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:31.210
is how I think about it.

00:11:32.265 --> 00:11:33.870
Let me just finish this then
I'll let you jump into it.

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:37.250
If I ran a workshop and
said okay, let's talk about

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:40.700
the demographics and
psychographics of your customers,

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:43.820
we'd probably have seven
or eight meaningful groups.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:48.150
Eventually it becomes too
small, but the first may be 18

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:51.880
to 23-year-old males, the
second one might be people

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:55.780
that make 80 thousand a
year, some may be in both.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:59.110
But once you get to those
eight, if you make two videos

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:02.960
per those eight, now you
have 16 assets and if you run

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:06.330
your media, which I think is
more efficient on Facebook.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:09.050
You see where I'm going,
how I spend that million

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:10.000
in a different way.

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:14.810
- [Man] Related question about the budget.

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:17.220
So one of the problems
that we econometric studies

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:19.310
about marketing efficiency
in Finland runs into

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:22.750
with digital is it's
hard to do digital a lot.

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:28.430
We have 95% brand awareness in Finland.

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:31.610
Our issue is ongoing into
areas where we would have

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:33.140
higher brand awareness.

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:40.910
Availability, opening hours,
group dynamics dictate

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.370
whether our marketing is efficient or not.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:48.980
The shops not open, if it's too
far, the queues are too long

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:51.430
on a Friday night, there's
very little we can do.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.420
Also, we sell to half of Finland.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:57.930
So we sell to a lot of
nurses and taxi drivers

00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.760
and unemployed people and what have you.

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:01.820
It might be an opportunity
from a segmentation

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:04.533
point of view, but the
point is how do you do

00:13:04.533 --> 00:13:06.520
social media marketing a lot?

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:10.620
We know that if we spend 50K on it easily

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:11.780
it'll be efficient.

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:13.720
But how do we spend half a million on it?

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:15.450
How do we spend 1.5 million on it?

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:17.540
That's what it runs to.

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:20.310
If it's awareness, our logo
needs to be everywhere,

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:22.990
our message needs to
be heard, that's fine.

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:26.430
But we only have so many times of the week

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:28.920
